course: dictionary
lesson: 10857
title: What a word feels like
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A vibe is the feeling or mood that a place, person or thing gives you. It is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk. «The vibe in here is cosy» tells you the room feels warm and comfortable, even if nobody says so.
explain: Context helps you spot the feeling. «Good vibes» means a happy, friendly feeling, and «bad vibes» means an unpleasant one. In a story, a character who «gets a weird vibe» senses that something feels wrong, like a warning.
explain: In slang, vibe is also a verb. To vibe means to relax and enjoy yourself, often to music, as in «just vibing». To vibe with someone means to get on well with them. Ask yourself: is this word describing a feeling, or an action?
fact: A vibe is a feeling or mood that a place, person or thing gives you.
fact: Vibe is informal, so it is best kept for casual talk rather than formal writing.
fact: «Good vibes» and «chill vibes» are calm, happy feelings; «bad vibes» is an unhappy feeling.
fact: To vibe means to relax and enjoy yourself, often to music; it is slang.
fact: Rarely, «vibes» is short for vibraphone, a musical instrument.
exercise: «The vibe in here is cosy.» What does vibe mean here? | A type of musical instrument | A loud noise from next door | A broken window | * The feeling or mood of the room
exercise: In a story, a girl «gets a weird vibe» about the old house. What does this suggest? | She has found a musical instrument | * Her feeling warns her that something is wrong | She is sure the house is brand new | Her feeling warns her that something is wrong
exercise: «We were just vibing to music all afternoon.» What does vibing mean? | Crossing a river | * Relaxing and enjoying yourself, often to music | Shouting at the radio | Working very hard on a test
test: Which phrase means a calm, relaxed feeling? | Heavy rain | A loud noise | * Chill vibes | Bad vibes
test: Mia says, «I vibe with Sam, we get on so well.» What does vibe with mean? | Race against | * Get on well with | Argue loudly with | Forget the name of
exam: In «Kai has the best vibes at our party», what does vibes most likely mean? | * The happy, friendly feeling he brings | The food on the plates | A drum kit | Kai's old bike
